      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, media framing often shifts based on the participants and the intensity of a protest. When groups are generally seen as less disruptive, the language might be more neutral or focused on their \"demands.\" Conversely, when demonstrations become more intense, vocabulary often changes to terms emphasizing disorder, conflict, or potential violence. This careful selection of words serves to shape the audience's overall perception of the event and the groups involved.",
